    "relief_ecs_education_mjWU74": {
      "type": "relief-ecs-education",
      "blocks": {
        "text_xCTebU": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Most people think CBD is just a wellness ingredient. What it actually is: a compound that interacts directly with your endocannabinoid system — a network of receptors (CB1 and CB2) found throughout your muscle tissue, joints, and connective tissue. But not all CBD is the same. The form it comes in changes everything.<br/></p>",
            "spacing": false
          }
        },
        "text_cMNhc8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>This system plays a direct role in how your body regulates physical tension and the recovery process after exertion or injury. CB2 receptors in particular are densely concentrated in areas of inflammation.</p>",
            "spacing": false
          }
        },
        "text_hUMLkW": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>The majority of CBD topicals on the market use <strong>isolate</strong>— pure, isolated CBD with every other compound stripped away. It's the cheapest form to produce and the most common. Some use <strong>broad spectrum</strong>, which adds terpenes and minor cannabinoids but removes all THC.</p>",
            "spacing": false
          }
        },
        "text_dJFLdM": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Max Relief uses <strong>full spectrum</strong>— the complete hemp plant profile. CBD, CBG, CBN, CBC, terpenes, flavonoids, and trace THC (&lt;0.3%). Research shows full spectrum produces up to 21% greater bioavailability than isolate or broad spectrum. The reason: the entourage effect — when all cannabinoids and terpenes work together, they enhance each other's absorption and effectiveness in ways that no single compound can replicate alone.</p>",
            "spacing": false
          }
        },
        "text_gYap4f": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><strong>And the concentration: </strong>Most topical CBD products deliver 3–5mg per ml. Max Relief delivers 20mg per ml — every size, every application. Full spectrum. Six times the concentration. Working with the system designed to manage it.</p>",
            "spacing": false
          }
        },
        "card_CeKrBN": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "⚡",
            "title": "Immediate — Lidocaine nerve block",
            "description": "Stops pain signals at the source while the deeper work begins underneath."
          }
        },
        "card_n4iaTk": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "🌱",
            "title": "Over time — CBD + endocannabinoid system",
            "description": "20mg/ml CBD binding to CB2 receptors in your tissue — consistent across every size. Builds with repeated use. Not just relief — recovery."
          }
        },
        "card_ygFB8r": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "🔄",
            "title": "Sustained — Botanicals + circulation",
            "description": "Arnica, Turmeric, and Clary Sage keep the recovery process moving after the immediate relief fades."
          }
        }
      },
